      ro: ["Yinchuan a fost capitala Imperiului Tangut (Xia de Vest) sub numele de Xingqing.", "Mormintele Xia de Vest cuprind 9 mausolee imperiale È™i peste 250 de morminte Ã®nsoÈ›itoare.", "Pagoda Haibao dateazÄƒ din secolul al V-lea È™i este una dintre cele mai vechi clÄƒdiri din oraÈ™.", "Ningxia produce peste 50% din vinurile premiate ale Chinei la nivel internaÈ›ional.", "Sistemul antic de canale din Yinchuan dateazÄƒ parÈ›ial din dinastiile Qin È™i Han.", "OraÈ™ul gÄƒzduieÈ™te China-Arab States Expo, un forum comercial internaÈ›ional major."],
      en: ["Yinchuan was the capital of the Western Xia Kingdom from 1038 until its conquest by Mongols.", "The Western Xia Tombs are often called the Pyramids of the East due to their unique shape.", "The 1,500-year-old Haibao Pagoda survived a major earthquake in 1739.", "The Helan Mountains contain thousands of ancient petroglyphs dating back 3,000 to 10,000 years.", "Yinchuan is the leading producer of wolfberries (goji berries) in the world.", "The city's Sand Lake (Sha Hu) is a rare landscape combining desert, lake, and reeds."],
