      ro: ["Taiyuan a fost fondat oficial Ã®n anul 497 Ã®.Hr. sub numele de oraÈ™ul Jinyang.", "Templul Jinci gÄƒzduieÈ™te 'Sala Mamei Sfinte', datÃ¢nd din dinastia Song (1023â€“1032).", "OraÈ™ul este cea mai mare bazÄƒ de producÈ›ie de oÈ›el inoxidabil din lume (TISCO).", "Taiyuan are o reÈ›ea extinsÄƒ de pagode istorice, inclusiv celebrele Pagode Gemene.", "OraÈ™ul a fost baza militarÄƒ a fondatorilor dinastiei Tang, Li Yuan È™i Li Shimin.", "Muzeul Shanxi din Taiyuan expune peste 400.000 de artefacte istorice È™i culturale."],
      en: ["Taiyuan was established in 497 BC, making it one of the oldest cities in northern China.", "The Hall of the Holy Mother at Jinci Temple features 43 realistic Song Dynasty clay statues.", "Taiyuan Iron and Steel (Group) Co., Ltd. (TISCO) is the largest stainless steel producer globally.", "The Twin Pagoda Temple (Yongzuo Temple) has been the city's emblem since the Ming Dynasty.", "Taiyuan was historically one of the three largest cities in northern China along with Luoyang and Xi'an.", "The city's Fen River Park is one of the largest ecological urban parks in China."],
