      hu: "ÃœrÃ¼mcsi, a Hszincsiang-Ujgur AutonÃ³m TerÃ¼let fÅ‘vÃ¡rosa a vilÃ¡g tengerektÅ‘l legtÃ¡volabb fekvÅ‘ nagyvÃ¡rosa vilÃ¡grekordjÃ¡t tartja. FÃ¶ldrajzilag EurÃ¡zsia szÃ­vÃ©ben, a Tien-san-hegysÃ©g Ã©szaki lejtÅ‘jÃ©n fekszik, Ã©s az Ã³kor Ã³ta a SelyemÃºt kÃ¶zponti csomÃ³pontjakÃ©nt szolgÃ¡l. ÃœrÃ¼mcsi neve az ojrÃ¡t nyelven 'szÃ©p legelÅ‘t' jelent. A vÃ¡ros a kultÃºrÃ¡k lenyÅ±gÃ¶zÅ‘ olvasztÃ³tÃ©gelye, ahol ujgurok, kazahok, hujok Ã©s han-kÃ­naiak Ã©lnek egyÃ¼tt, ami a Nagy BazÃ¡r Ã©pÃ­tÃ©szetÃ©ben Ã©s a helyi piacok sokszÃ­nÅ±sÃ©gÃ©ben is megmutatkozik. A legfontosabb kulturÃ¡lis lÃ¡tnivalÃ³k kÃ¶zÃ© tartozik a Hszincsiangi RegionÃ¡lis MÃºzeum, vilÃ¡ghÃ­rÅ± Tarim-medencei mÃºmiÃ¡ival. ÃœrÃ¼mcsi ma modern ipari Ã©s logisztikai kÃ¶zpont, amely Ã¶sszekÃ¶ti KÃ­nÃ¡t KÃ¶zÃ©p-ÃzsiÃ¡val Ã©s EurÃ³pÃ¡val. KÃ¶zvetlen kÃ¶zelÃ©ben talÃ¡lhatÃ³ a Mennyei-tÃ³ (Tianchi), egy lÃ¡tvÃ¡nyos alpesi tÃ³ hÃ³fÃ¶dte csÃºcsokkal a hÃ¡ttÃ©rben. A vÃ¡ros a rÃ©giÃ³ olaj-, gÃ¡z- Ã©s textiliparÃ¡nak kÃ¶zpontja is.",
      ro: "ÃœrÃ¼mqi, capitala Regiunii Autonome Xinjiang-Uygur, deÈ›ine recordul mondial ca fiind cel mai Ã®ndepÄƒrtat oraÈ™ mare de orice mare sau ocean. Din punct de vedere geografic, este situat Ã®n inima Eurasiei, pe versantul nordic al munÈ›ilor Tianshan, servind ca un nod central al Drumului MÄƒtÄƒsii Ã®ncÄƒ din antichitate. Numele ÃœrÃ¼mqi Ã®nseamnÄƒ 'PÄƒÈ™une FrumoasÄƒ' Ã®n limba oirat. OraÈ™ul este un amestec fascinant de culturi, unde trÄƒiesc Ã®mpreunÄƒ uigurii, kazaÈ™ii, chinezii Hui È™i Han, fapt reflectat Ã®n arhitectura Marelui Bazar È™i Ã®n diversitatea pieÈ›elor locale. Printre cele mai importante atracÈ›ii culturale se numÄƒrÄƒ Muzeul Regional Xinjiang, cu mumiile sale celebre din Bazinul Tarim. AstÄƒzi, ÃœrÃ¼mqi este un centru industrial È™i logistic modern care leagÄƒ China de Asia CentralÄƒ È™i Europa. ÃŽn imediata apropiere se aflÄƒ Lacul Heavenly (Tianchi), un lac alpin spectaculos situat Ã®n faÈ›a vÃ¢rfurilor Ã®nzÄƒpezite. OraÈ™ul este, de asemenea, un centru pentru industria petrolului, gazelor È™i textilelor din regiune.",
      en: "ÃœrÃ¼mqi, the capital of the Xinjiang Uyghur Autonomous Region, holds the Guinness World Record for being the most remote major city from any sea. Geographically nestled in the heart of Eurasia on the northern slopes of the Tianshan Mountains, it has functioned as a vital hub on the Silk Road for over two millennia. Its name means Beautiful Pasture in the Oirat language, contrasting with its modern identity as a sprawling industrial metropolis. ÃœrÃ¼mqi is a profound cultural crossroads where Uyghur, Kazakh, Hui, and Han Chinese traditions merge, most notably seen at the Grand Bazaar, one of the largest Islamic-style markets in the world. The Xinjiang Regional Museum is a key attraction, housing the exceptionally preserved Tarim mummies dating back nearly 4,000 years. Today, ÃœrÃ¼mqi is a cornerstone of China's Belt and Road Initiative, linking the nation with Central Asia and Europe via rail and road. Nearby, the Tianchi (Heavenly Lake) offers stunning alpine scenery amid snow-capped peaks.",
