      hu: "Lhasza, a Tibeti AutonÃ³m TerÃ¼let kÃ¶zigazgatÃ¡si Ã©s spirituÃ¡lis kÃ¶zpontja, kÃ¶rÃ¼lbelÃ¼l 3650 mÃ©teres tengerszint feletti magassÃ¡gban fekszik a HimalÃ¡ja hegyvonulatai kÃ¶zÃ¶tt. A vÃ¡ros tÃ¶bb mint 1300 Ã©ves mÃºltra tekint vissza, a 7. szÃ¡zadban Szongcen Gampo tette a Tibeti Birodalom fÅ‘vÃ¡rosÃ¡vÃ¡. Legismertebb jelkÃ©pe a Potala-palota, amely a Dalai LÃ¡mÃ¡k egykori tÃ©li rezidenciÃ¡jakÃ©nt magasodik a vÃ¡ros fÃ¶lÃ©. A politikai jelentÅ‘sÃ©g mellett Lhasza a buddhista hÃ­vÅ‘k legfontosabb zarÃ¡ndokhelye, kÃ¶zpontjÃ¡ban a Barkhor negyed Ã©s a szent Jokhang-templom talÃ¡lhatÃ³. A Lhasza-folyÃ³ vÃ¶lgyÃ©ben elterÃ¼lÅ‘ telepÃ¼lÃ©s Ã©ghajlata napfÃ©nyes, de ritka a levegÅ‘, ami meghatÃ¡rozza a mindennapi Ã©letvitelt. A modern infrastrukturÃ¡lis fejlesztÃ©sek, pÃ©ldÃ¡ul a vilÃ¡g legmagasabban fekvÅ‘ vasÃºtvonala, szorosabbÃ¡ tettÃ©k a kapcsolatot KÃ­na tÃ¶bbi rÃ©szÃ©vel, mikÃ¶zben a vÃ¡ros megÅ‘rizte egyedÃ¼lÃ¡llÃ³ kulturÃ¡lis Ã©s vallÃ¡si jellegÃ©t.",
      ro: "Lhasa, centrul administrativ È™i spiritual al Regiunii Autonome Tibet, este situat la o altitudine de aproximativ 3.650 de metri Ã®n munÈ›ii Himalaya. OraÈ™ul are o istorie de peste 1.300 de ani, fiind stabilit drept capitalÄƒ a Imperiului Tibetan Ã®n secolul al VII-lea de cÄƒtre Songtsen Gampo. Cel mai emblematic monument este Palatul Potala, fosta reÈ™edinÈ›Äƒ de iarnÄƒ a lui Dalai Lama, care dominÄƒ peisajul urban de pe dealul Marpo Ri. Pe lÃ¢ngÄƒ importanÈ›a sa politicÄƒ, Lhasa rÄƒmÃ¢ne cel mai sfÃ¢nt loc de pelerinaj pentru budiÈ™tii tibetani, centrul spiritual fiind Templul Jokhang din cartierul Barkhor. PoziÈ›ionarea sa geograficÄƒ Ã®n valea rÃ¢ului Lhasa influenÈ›eazÄƒ climatul arid È™i Ã®nsorit, dar È™i arhitectura tradiÈ›ionalÄƒ adaptatÄƒ la altitudine. ÃŽn prezent, oraÈ™ul trece printr-un proces rapid de modernizare, integrÃ¢ndu-se Ã®n reÈ›eaua feroviarÄƒ È™i economicÄƒ a Chinei, pÄƒstrÃ¢nd totodatÄƒ o atmosferÄƒ culturalÄƒ unicÄƒ Ã®n lume.",
      en: "Lhasa, the administrative and spiritual heart of the Tibet Autonomous Region, is situated at an altitude of approximately 3,650 meters in the Himalayan highlands. The city boasts a history spanning over 1,300 years, having been established as the capital of the Tibetan Empire in the 7th century by Songtsen Gampo. Its most iconic landmark is the Potala Palace, the former winter residence of the Dalai Lama, which stands majestically atop Marpo Ri hill. Beyond its political status, Lhasa is the premier pilgrimage destination for Buddhists, centered around the Jokhang Temple and the bustling Barkhor circuit. The city's geography in the Lhasa River valley dictates its sunny yet thin-aired climate, shaping the lifestyle of its residents. Modern infrastructure projects, including the high-altitude Qinghai-Tibet railway, have transformed its connectivity, while the city continues to serve as the definitive cultural anchor for Tibetan heritage.",
