      en: "Kunming, the capital of Yunnan Province, is celebrated globally as the 'City of Eternal Spring' due to its mild, year-round temperate climate. Located on the northern shore of Lake Dian at an elevation of about 1,900 meters, it serves as a vital gateway between China and Southeast Asia. Kunming's history dates back over 2,000 years, flourishing during the Dali Kingdom era and later expanding under the Ming Dynasty. Today, the city is a premier center for horticulture, home to one of Asia's largest flower markets which underpins much of its local economy. Culturally, Kunming is defined by its rich ethnic diversity, as Yunnan is home to numerous minority groups whose influence is evident in the city's architecture and cuisine. The surrounding natural wonders, particularly the Shilin Stone Forest, make the region a major destination for nature-based tourism. Kunming seamlessly integrates modern urban infrastructure with the relaxed pace of life typical of China's southwestern highlands.",
